<code>assert element != null => this.peek() == element;</code>

This assert statement checks that if the element added to the queue is not null, then the element at the front of the queue (which is the last element added due to the nature of the circular FIFO queue) is equal to the element that was just added.
--------------------
<code>assert element != null => element.equals(this.peek());</code>
--------------------
<code>assert element != null => element.equals(this.peek());</code>

This assertion reflects the condition that if the element added is not null, it will be the last element in the queue after the operation, which is accessed via the `peek()` method.
